# Architecture Analysis for C4 Diagrams

## Overall Context

This is the **BA Holidays "Darwin" platform** — a greenfield holidays booking system for British Airways Holidays. It is organised into two main bounded contexts: **Search & Browse** and **Checkout & Pay**, plus a shared **Payments Platform**.

The stack is Kotlin/Java Spring Boot + Next.js, deployed on **AWS ECS** (EC2 instances), routed through **Kong API Gateway**, fronted by **Akamai CDN/WAF**.

---

## System Context (C4 Level 1)

| External Actor/System | Role |
|---|---|
| **Customer / Traveller** | Books holidays via `holiday.britishairways.com` or `www.holidays.britishairways.com` |
| **Akamai CDN/WAF** | Edge layer; forwards traffic to Kong data planes |
| **TravelBox (Codegen)** | External reservation management system (hotel+bundle booking engine) |
| **Amadeus NDC API** | External flight shopping SOAP API (NDC standard via `nodeA3.test.webservices.amadeus.com`) |
| **IAGL EI (External Interface)** | BA's B2B/NDC flight booking API (SOAP: `/v2/AirBookPortType`) |
| **Avios / IAG Loyalty** | Loyalty programme — issues/redeems Avios points (`api.iagloyalty.com`) |
| **CyberSource** | Visa/MC/Amex payment gateway (merchant: `iaglppbah`) |
| **PCI Proxy (Datatrans)** | Card tokenization proxy (PCI compliance) |
| **Sycurio** | Phone-channel / PBX payment service |
| **Contentful** | Headless CMS for search/browse content |
| **Auth0** | Customer authentication (OIDC) |
| **DevCycle** | Feature flags SaaS |
| **Google Maps** | Maps API (destination display) |
| **Datadog** | Observability — logs, traces, metrics |
| **OpenJaw (BAH Classic)** | Legacy redirect for non-Darwin destinations (BAH_BADP_ENCRYPTION_KEY) |
| **AMEX** | Creates Virtual Credit Cards (via DSPI) |
| **HolidayTaxis (HTX)** | Airport transfers provider (`HTX_API_TOKEN`) |

