## Key User Journeys (for QA reference)

### 1. Search and Browse Flow
```
Customer -> Akamai -> Kong (S&B Account)
  -> Presentation Shell [loads Search & Select MFE via Module Federation]
  -> Search MFE calls BFF: GET /api/search/v1/accommodation
  -> BFF -> TravelBox (hotel offers + pricing)
  -> BFF -> NDC Connector -> Amadeus SOAP (flight prices)
  -> BFF -> Valkey (cache result)
  <- Returns combined hotel + flight offers to UI
```

### 2. Checkout and Booking Flow
```
Customer selects offer
  -> Shell -> Kong (C&P Account, cross-account) -> Checkout Backend
  -> Checkout -> TravelBox (lock offer / create cart)
  -> Checkout -> Avios (price in points, if applicable)
  -> Customer submits payment
  -> Checkout -> Payments Orchestrator (same C&P Account)
    -> Orchestrator -> PCI Proxy (tokenise card)
    -> Orchestrator -> CyberSource (authorise and capture)
    [or Orchestrator -> Avios (redeem points)]
  <- Payment success
  -> Checkout -> TravelBox (confirm booking)
  -> Checkout -> Flight Orders Adapter -> IAGL EI (create flight order)
  <- Booking reference returned to customer
```

### 3. Manage Booking Flow
```
Customer -> Akamai -> Kong (S&B Account)
  -> Kong proxies /mf_provider_booking/* -> Manage Trip Account (cross-account)
  -> Presentation Shell loads Manage Trip MFE [Module Federation, cross-account]
  -> Manage Trip MFE -> Manage Trip BFF (Manage Trip Account)
  -> Manage Trip BFF -> TravelBox (retrieve booking details)
  <- Booking details shown to customer
```

### 4. Supplier Payment Flow (post-booking, internal, C&P Account)
```
Booking confirmed
  -> FSI reads DynamoDB (booking record)
  -> FSI -> Aurora PostgreSQL (financial transaction record)
  -> DSPI -> AMEX (create Virtual Credit Card for hotel supplier)
  -> DSPI -> Aurora PostgreSQL (store VCC data)
```
